following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T13:30:46Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T13:30:46Z","body":"Does the font really need to update part of the texture?\nCan't it create an image on CPU, compose the font on CPU Image, then upload it as a single texture?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940057697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043937347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104537#issuecomment-3043937347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104537","id":3043937347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61bsxD","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T08:18:29Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T08:18:29Z","body":"> Can't it create an image on CPU, compose the font on CPU Image, then upload it as a single texture?\n\nIt is already doing this when possible, but new used glyphs are often added dynamically and font can't know which will be used in advance.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043937347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044397413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104537#issuecomment-3044397413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104537","id":3044397413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61ddFl","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T10:35:32Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T10:39:06Z","body":"> It is already doing this when possible, but new used glyphs are often added dynamically and font can't know which will be used in advance.\n\nAh I get you.\n\nThen as @clayjohn says support for partial texture updates does sound an obvious thing to explore, if 4.x doesn't offer this already. There's probably a few gotchas afaik, like probably using uncompressed format (i.e. aiming to avoid recompress if possible as that is super slow), and generating mipmaps.\n\nThe other trick for this (if you have to use multiple textures) is item re-ordering in the batching, which 3.x supports. There are two subtle aspects though, overlap test (which can get expensive in the case of characters with float widths which might just overlap on boundaries), or offering no-overlap guarantee to the batching.\n\nYou could also possibly do all this on the scene side _before_ passing the text to the rendering server. As text often doesn't vary per frame, it makes sense to do as much as possible as a one-off, rather than per frame.\n\nIn 3.x we have `MultiRect`, so you would e.g. compose a multirect for a bunch of characters using the same texture, then a bunch of characters using 2nd texture etc. I don't know if 4.x ever got multirect, but you could do similar groupings.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044397413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044438136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104537#issuecomment-3044438136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104537","id":3044438136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61dnB4","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T10:45:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T10:47:36Z","body":"> if 4.x doesn't offer this already.\n\nIt's not (there are old draft PR, but it's outdated, was done before Metal and D3D12 was added).\n\n> The other trick for this (if you have to use multiple textures) is item re-ordering in the batching\n\n4.x is using batching, but it will not work in all cases, since renderer have no idea if draw order is relevant.\n\n> I changed it to draw a whole bunch of shadows, then all the characters on top, so no texture / shader changes.\n\nAll text draw cases already do this, the issue is mostly caused by multiple fonts and multiple textures per-font, not shadows/outlines.\n\n> You could also possibly do all this on the scene side before passing the text to the rendering server. As text often doesn't vary per frame, it makes sense to do as much as possible as a one-off, rather than per frame.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108369 does this, pre-sorts draw calls where order is irrelevant and improve batching a lot.\n\nHaving partial updates is still desired, single texture is always better than multiple.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044438136/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]